From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pid: honor fixed fan duty at the final PWM output

SetFan represents fixed duty as equal OutLimitMin/OutLimitMax values in
the supported 10..100 percent range. The later zone failsafe adjustment
must not raise that explicit per-fan command. Derive the output directly
from valid fixed limits and keep zone failure detection and diagnostics
active. Adaptive fans in the same zone still use the normal failsafe PWM.

Base: phosphor-pid-control f6d4cb9e5ddaeb14fbd14f9d5730fd71afe8efe2
plus CEB-GNRD patches 0001..0004.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD fixed fan control policy]

diff --git a/pid/fancontroller.cpp b/pid/fancontroller.cpp
--- a/pid/fancontroller.cpp
+++ b/pid/fancontroller.cpp
@@ -123,7 +123,14 @@
 
 void FanController::outputProc(double value)
 {
-    double percent = value;
+    // CEB-GNRD SetFan encodes a fixed 10..100% duty using equal output
+    // limits. Honor that per-controller command at the final PWM output,
+    // including while shared zone inputs report a critical/failsafe state.
+    // Reject invalid/uninitialized limits so they cannot disable failsafe.
+    const auto& limits = getPIDInfo()->outLim;
+    const bool fixedDuty = std::isfinite(limits.min) && limits.min >= 10.0 &&
+                           limits.min <= 100.0 && limits.min == limits.max;
+    double percent = fixedDuty ? limits.min : value;
 
     /* If doing tuning, don't go into failsafe mode. */
     if (!tuningEnabled)
@@ -137,7 +144,7 @@
             failsafeTransition = true;
         }
 
-        if (failsafeCurrState)
+        if (failsafeCurrState && !fixedDuty)
         {
             double failsafePercent = _owner->getFailSafePercent();
 
